//Skirt: cream overskirt in two side pieces, caught up by bows at the front and the back
# Overskirt: on each side a cream piece from 34 to 142 degrees, just outside the skirt
# (osr). Each end is caught up by a bow; the hem (ozh, a spline through points measured on the front and back
# views) hangs straight down the front edge from the bow to 4.3, swags to 2.95 at the side and rises up the
# back to 4.5 under the back bow; the cloth falls in folds that deepen toward the hem. q runs across a piece from
# the front bow to the back bow, p down from the waist to the hem. Lined in orange, with the hem turned
# back over the side (oft) so the lining shows there, as drawn on the sheet.
osr(h)=sa(sz(h))+0.17*min(1,max(0,8.2-h)/0.3)
ozh(q)=4.30062+(-2.93914)*q+79.80551*max(0,q-0.00021)^3+(-228.56574)*max(0,q-0.07114)^3+286.31321*max(0,q-0.12714)^3+(-211.82871)*max(0,q-0.16448)^3+(-1590.50757)*max(0,q-0.21114)^3+4357.47227*max(0,q-0.24848)^3+(-1712.36965)*max(0,q-0.27648)^3+(-1545.84217)*max(0,q-0.30448)^3+590.477*max(0,q-0.37914)^3+(-49.4433)*max(0,q-0.56581)^3+265.23117*max(0,q-0.70581)^3+(-847.35342)*max(0,q-0.78048)^3+1258.08921*max(0,q-0.82248)^3+(-1030.93157)*max(0,q-0.86447)^3+(-936.88051)*max(0,q-0.90181)^3+3400.58277*max(0,q-0.92981)^3+(-3316.24082)*max(0,q-0.96247)^3+555.91711*max(0,q-0.98114)^3+676.07521*max(0,q-0.99981)^3
oph(q,p)=8.2-(8.2-ozh(q))*p
ofd(q,p)=0.1*p^1.2*(0.5+0.5*sin(10*pi*q))
oft(q)=0.26*sin(pi*q)^3
